spb = 60 / song.bpm / song.steps;\n370:        f.type = 'bandpass'; f.Q.value = 1.8; f.frequency.value = 650 + (i % 4) * 160;\n# Deduplicated findings\n\nOnly observed findings are counted. Driver fixture mistakes are recorded separately in test notes and do not inflate the game issue count. Severity is based on player impact; a missing visual ring is high, and a file that cannot boot is critical.\n\n| ID | Severity | Detection | Finding | Resolution |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| UI001 | Critical | Emitted HTML browser launch | A malformed destination-menu closure prevented the UI module from parsing and blocked boot. | Fixed delimiter; final-file title → selection → courtyard smoke passes. |\n| SIM001 | Medium | Continue event-identity assertion | Restored history could reuse old event ids, suppressing deduplicated sound/visual cues. | Preserve monotonic event identities across checkpoint restoration. |\n| SIM002 | Medium | Deterministic director event test | A Ringmaster shift selection only set a transient warning and did not schedule a movement. | Schedule warned authored partition shift. |\n| VIEW001 | Medium | Native screenshots | Original shapes faced edge-on to the three-quarter camera. | Use native south-facing orientation for authored shapes. |\n| VIEW002 | Medium | Map screenshot | The queued table hid route decals and northern tokens. | Correct depth biases and token placement. |\n| VIEW003 | Medium | Finale screenshot | The initial hero camera cropped the dragon and northern stations. | Bespoke final framing includes dragon, cover and all four stations. |\n| VIEW004 | High | Ring-drop visual review | A picked-up then dropped ring could disappear because rendering checked the historical pickup flag. | Draw every uncarried, unsecured ring. |\n| AUDIO001 | Low | Event integration review + spy test | Numeric hero ids hid class identity from kit sound selection. | Select by `classId` and test each kit’s effect mapping. |\n| UI002 | Low | 1920 × 1080 courtyard 