{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat Quest-for-the-Fourfold-Rings-Quest-for-the-Rings-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031849/docs/browser-findings.md && cat Quest-for-the-Fourfold-Rings-Quest-for-the-Rings-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031849/docs/sim-findings.md && ls -lh Quest-for-the-Fourfold-Rings-Quest-for-the-Rings-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031849/evidence'","aggregated_output":"# Browser evidence\n\nFinal HTML tested through file://. Detailed current results: evidence/browser.json.\n\n- single emitted HTML boots file:// with pinned native renderer: PASS\n- clean-profile actual music default is ten percent: PASS\n- title buttons and disabled Continue are usable: PASS\n- mouse hover moves native menu focus: PASS\n- help explains solo/couch/Hub and every mandatory touch action: PASS\n- attract never starts over Settings: PASS\n- native settings exposes independent music, SFX, voice and comfort: PASS\n- About has all four required feedback categories: PASS\n- source information is backed by parsed builder interview: PASS\n- four selectable animated native hero rigs exist: PASS\n- new expedition gives one human and useful AI companion: PASS\n- real keyboard movement changes authoritative position: PASS\n- mouse primary uses ordinary combat and switches prompts: PASS\n- mouse aim transforms camera and native view correctly: PASS\n- keyboard class power and dodge use live kit rules: PASS\n- standard pad hot-switch shows PlayStation glyphs: PASS\n- Xbox glyph setting changes context prompt: PASS\n- free second standard controller joins safely from courtyard: PASS\n- secondary disconnect pauses with reconnect choice: PASS\n- actual returning controller resumes its human hero: PASS\n- Continue with AI transfers secondary ownership without stranding run: PASS\n- pad Options opens standalone pause: PASS\n- standalone pause stops simulation without charging Dread: PASS\n- Dev Mode exposes complete tuning registry bounds: PASS\n- pad adjusts focused live tuning slider: PASS\n- live slider mutation marks run assisted: PASS\n- Reset to Defaults restores tuning registry safely: PASS\n- ordinary input driver reaches courtyard waystone: PASS\n- castle entry charges Dread exactly once: PASS\n- ordinary input retrieves oath-ring and extracts room one: PASS\n- moving to room two does not charge entry again: PASS\n- safe transition checkpoint contains room two and charged Dread: PASS\n- Continue enabled after a real safe checkpoint: PASS\n- Continue restores room, classes and Dread without re-entry charge: PASS\n- rendering remains observational for authoritative state: PASS\n- native controls screen lists rebindable primary action: PASS\n- native key rebinding updates the primary action map: PASS\n- native crystal2 visual scenario has no engine errors: PASS\n- native inferno2 visual scenario has no engine errors: PASS\n- native shifting2 visual scenario has no engine errors: PASS\n- native final visual scenario has no engine errors: PASS\n- all native authored enemies draw finite coordinates for string IDs: PASS\n- played escape reaches ending and replay options: PASS\n- attract does not start before ten seconds: PASS\n- attract starts at ten-second idle threshold: PASS\n- attract loop covers all geometry families and dragon: PASS\n- attract never writes checkpoint progress: PASS\n- any keyboard input exits demo and is consumed: PASS\n- pointer exits attract without selecting title action: PASS\n- pad exits attract without selecting title action: PASS\n- file launch makes no missing neighboring requests: PASS\n- integrated desktop has no console/page/engine exceptions: PASS\n- malformed checkpoint is rejected without Continue trap: PASS\n- malformed storage degrades gracefully and can start a new run: PASS\n- outdated checkpoint is rejected without Continue trap: PASS\n- outdated storage degrades gracefully and can start a new run: PASS\n- blocked checkpoint is rejected without Continue trap: PASS\n- blocked storage degrades gracefully and can start a new run: PASS\n- full storage degrades gracefully and can start a new run: PASS\n- iPhone 13 simultaneous invisible movement and aim sticks: PASS\n- iPhone 13 contextual class power reachable while moving: PASS\n- iPhone 13 cancelled pointers release movement: PASS\n- iPhone 13 ordinary route works at touch viewport: PASS\n- iPhone 13 contact-sensitive touch pickup takes shared ring: PASS\n- iPhone 13 touch extraction reaches second authored room: PASS\n- iPhone 13 landscape resize keeps native rendering and safe document bounds: PASS\n- iPad Pro 11 simultaneous invisible movement and aim sticks: PASS\n- iPad Pro 11 contextual class power reachable while moving: PASS\n- iPad Pro 11 cancelled pointers release movement: PASS\n- iPad Pro 11 ordinary route works at touch viewport: PASS\n- iPad Pro 11 contact-sensitive touch pickup takes shared ring: PASS\n- iPad Pro 11 touch extraction reaches second authored room: PASS\n- iPad Pro 11 landscape resize keeps native rendering and safe document bounds: PASS\n- webkit native file boot and gameplay: PASS\n- firefox native file boot and gameplay: PASS\n\nPhysical hardware and remote-human behavior remain unknown. Gamepads and touch hardware were emulated; all screenshots with development setup are labeled assisted.\n# Simulation findings\n\nOnly actual game findings count below. Two initial test fixture mistakes (a fixture missing its site context, and a test comparing different positions in an RNG sequence) were corrected in tests and are not counted as game defects.\n\n| ID | Severity | Finding | Evidence | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SIM-001 | Medium | Continue restores historical events but restarts event IDs, allowing collisions with prior events and suppressing consumers that deduplicate IDs. | `Continue keeps event identities monotonic after checkpoint` fails: a post-restore pickup ID is below the maximum pre-save historical ID. | Fixed and regression test passes. |\n| SIM-002 | Medium | A Ringmaster shift event spends its finite budget but its warning is erased on the next hazard update and no partition shift is scheduled. | Deterministic `rule-fixture-shifting1` seed selects shift at 14s; warning is false at 14.02s, before its telegraph can complete. Test `Ringmaster shift event telegraphs then moves an authored partition`. | Fixed and regression test passes. |\n\nAdditional resolved findings:\n\n- SIM-003 (low, caught while adding the timeline regression test): a partial aim input containing `ax` but no `ay` passed the magnitude check and then called `atan2(undefined, ax)`, making authoritative facing and projectiles non-finite. Missing aim axes now normalize to zero; the finite-facing regression passes.\n- SIM-004 (medium, root integration-review finding): cloaked contact damage applied only to flying Nightmares and occurred after target selection, so other families and the both-hidden/no-target branch could silently grant contact immunity. Contact now applies to every awake family (including the stationary dragon) before target selection, while existing stun/dodge/guard/hurt rules remain in force. A five-family both-hidden contact regression passes.\n\n- SIM-005 (high, root objective-review finding): a noncarrier waiting at the exit could trigger delivery while the actual ring carrier remained elsewhere. Exit context now belongs to the carrier and completion independently verifies a living carrier at the gate. Final escape also requires every living hero to regroup; a downed partner remains recoverable. Four regression checks prove rejection, real carrier delivery, shared final regroup and survivor rescue.\n- SIM-006 (medium, integration-review finding): Continue discarded the assisted-run label and live tuning, potentially presenting a previously assisted expedition as normal. Checkpoints now retain both; malformed tuning/statistics are rejected and older optional fields remain compatible. Three regression checks cover this.\n\nNo critical/game-breaking blocker has been found by these simulation tests so far; SIM-005 was a high-severity objective bypass. A normal full expedition and all ten unordered class pairs reach victory without debug mutations. Those outcomes do not prove subjective balance or a 20–30-minute human playtime.\n\n## Current automated coverage\n\n`tests/simulation.mjs` exports `runSimulationTests()` returning result objects; `tests/playthrough.mjs` exports `runPlaythroughTests()` and a reusable `ordinaryExpedition()` input driver. Integrate these behind `node tools/test.mjs`; test files are not bundled. Evidence is in `evidence/simulation.json` and `evidence/playthrough.json`.\n\nThe current suite has 89 passing checks: all authored geometry/partition states, route ownership/Dread, native attack timing, all four kits, ward/dodge/guard, status constraints, treasure pickup/pass/drop/recovery, revive priority and interruption, extraction of a downed partner, shifting safety, companion rescue in four families and visible safe stuck recovery, Continue/retry, corrupted saves, caches, final wipe/reset, labeled RNG, snapshots and director budgets, plus ten complete ordinary class-pair expeditions.\n\nThe separate normal expedition includes both optional caches. It records the actual action sequence, health samples, room transitions, seed, and an independent event history proving eight core room completions, four unique secured rings, four distinct seal stations and one victory. It uses default health/resources, no debug commands, no room jumps, no direct ring/objective state mutations, and no invulnerability.\n\n\n## Integration corrections\n\nEvery hero now uses a distinct existing native Attack move: Warrior `slash`, Wizard `cast`, Phantom `rising`, Changeling `throw`. Explicit `.15s` wind-up, `.18s` active phase, `.35` active hit fraction and live recovery tuning are shared by animation, effect release and action sound. The three non-damaging actions release once at the active threshold; clients reconstruct the same native spec. Four class-specific timing tests verify that wind-up produces no spell/lure/reveal or attack sound, and that active releases exactly one.\n\nA Ringmaster partition action schedules a real shift after its full warning rather than setting a transient visual flag. A phase offset integrates this authored event with regular partition timing without snapping the wall back on the following tick. Warning state is replicated to clients.\n\nCheckpoints retain event IDs, ticks, epochs and labeled RNG state; older version-3 checkpoints safely recover their event counters from validated history. New events stay monotonic. Snapshot tuning transmits deviations from defaults and clients combine defaults with those deviations, reducing repeated packet data while making Reset to Defaults propagate correctly.\n\n\nLatest relevant command: `node tools/test.mjs simulation playthrough audio` → **108 passed, 0 failed** (84 simulation, 2 playthrough, 22 audio). This rerun uses the corrected extraction/shared-escape and checkpoint rules. All ten ordinary class-pair expeditions and the full two-cache expedition still reach victory without a debug mutation or objective teleport. The normal bot required no regroup workaround.\n\n\n## Final integration audit corrections\n\n- SIM-007 (medium, integration-review finding): possession projections stored a copied `classId` but every class used a generic melee attack. Echoes now reuse the copied kit's action family: a Warrior's melee, Wizard's warned fixed-aim hostile rune, Phantom's warned reveal/repulsion pulse, or Changeling's one finite decoy. Wind-ups are intentionally longer for hostile readability. Projections never take input ownership or create recursive enemies. Four regression checks cover fixed aim and timing, pulse safety/single release, finite decoy/team replication, and visible-hero contact danger.\n- SIM-008 (high, root network-review finding): host-created development hazard lanes damaged players, but snapshots sent only their phase list and clients reconstructed only the authored static lanes. Compact extra hazard definitions now accompany phase state. One regression checks equal host/client geometry, period, phase and warning progress.\n\nLatest affected-suite command: `node tools/test.mjs simulation playthrough` → **91 passed, 0 failed** (89 simulation + 2 playthrough). All ten ordinary class pairs and the full two-cache expedition still finish under the current echo rules. Audio code was unchanged by these fixes, so its prior 22 passing assertions were not repeated for reassurance.\ntotal 13M\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha 4.0K Nov  6 03:33 assets\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 5.7K Nov  6 03:33 assets-report.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 4.5K Nov  6 03:45 audio.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 144K Nov  6 03:54 browser-attract.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 301K Nov  6 03:53 browser-board.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 586K Nov  6 03:54 browser-controls.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 294K Nov  6 03:53 browser-courtyard.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 295K Nov  6 03:54 browser-crystal2-assisted.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 283K Nov  6 03:53 browser-dev-mode.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 294K Nov  6 03:54 browser-dungeon-normal.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 315K Nov  6 03:54 browser-final-assisted.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 237K Nov  6 03:54 browser-firefox-native.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1.5M Nov  6 03:53 browser-help.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  96K Nov  6 03:53 browser-hero-selection.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 292K Nov  6 03:54 browser-inferno2-assisted.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 186K Nov  6 03:54 browser-ipad-pro-11-landscape.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 209K Nov  6 03:54 browser-ipad-pro-11.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 288K Nov  6 03:54 browser-iphone-13-landscape.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 281K Nov  6 03:54 browser-iphone-13.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1.2M Nov  6 03:53 browser-settings.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 299K Nov  6 03:54 browser-shifting2-assisted.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 110K Nov  6 03:53 browser-source-information.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 808K Nov  6 03:53 browser-title.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 429K Nov  6 03:54 browser-victory-assisted.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 159K Nov  6 03:54 browser-webkit-native.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  13K Nov  6 03:54 browser.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 281K Nov  6 03:38 courtyard-initial.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 2.0M Nov  6 03:53 hub-campaign.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  22K Nov  6 03:38 hub-conformance.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 149K Nov  6 03:44 hub-gameplay.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1007 Nov  6 03:52 integration.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  595 Nov  6 03:38 partition-report.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 543K Nov  6 03:53 playthrough.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  15K Nov  6 03:53 simulation.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  217 Nov  6 03:54 test-last.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 808K Nov  6 03:38 title-initial.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  377 Nov  6 03:54 touch-menu-audit.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  68K Nov  6 03:38 view-board.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  94K Nov  6 03:38 view-crystal2.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  95K Nov  6 03:38 view-dungeon2.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 126K Nov  6 03:38 view-final.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 101K Nov  6 03:38 view-inferno2.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  96K Nov  6 03:38 view-shifting2.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 101K Nov  6 03:38 view-title.png\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
