{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_110","type":"agent_message","text":"Built [**Quest for the Fourfold Rings**](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-031849__x044b4b/work/Quest-for-the-Fourfold-Rings-Quest-for-the-Rings-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-031849.html). Open the HTML directly in a browser.\n\n**343 checks passed, 0 failed**, including all ten hero pairings and a complete server-hosted online expedition.\n\n[Builder interview](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-031849__x044b4b/work/exit-interview.json) · [Progress and completion record](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra.build-v2__20261106-031849__x044b4b/work/PROGRESS.md)\n\n**Source Information:** Date: 2026-11-06 03:18:49. Source: *Quest for the Rings* (1981). Plan: PLAN.md. Genre: cooperative fantasy action-adventure. Perspective: fixed three-quarter. Tech: JavaScript, HTML/CSS, Canvas 2D, my-3D2dge 0.89.1, AI Hub client 1.4.0. Art: original native procedural pixel assets. Animation: continuous rigs and native Attack timelines. Audio: code-only music, effects and gibberish; music defaults to 10%. Online: solo companion, couch co-op and AI Hub shared-world co-op for 1–2 players. Testing: headless simulation, Chromium/WebKit/Firefox, emulated controllers/touch, offline audio and Hub scenarios. Research: [original manual](https://odyssey2.info/library/manuals/us_questfortherings/quest-for-the-rings.txt), [illustrated scans](https://odyssey2.info/library/library_view.php?i=53), pinned engine and protocol documentation. Environment: Codex CLI, headless Linux/WSL2. Model: OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort ultra. Usage: **added on import**. Physical-device performance, subjective audio quality and first-player pacing remain unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback**, in the required order:\n\n1. Found and fixed 30 distinct defects through tests, visual checks and integration review.\n2. One initial critical boot blocker; fixed.\n3. Most helpful: ordinary-input whole campaign with server-only authority and two clients.\n4. Least helpful: screenshots captured before menu fades settled.\n\n**Engine Feedback**, in the required order:\n\n1. Best feature: shaded procedural assets and continuous character rigs.\n2. Initial mistakes involved shape facing, depth ordering and camera framing.\n3. Largest custom system: the cooperative expedition simulation and authoritative replication.\n4. Hardest part: keeping changing geometry, collision, animation and client presentation consistent.\n5. Engine source changes: none; extended its native registries and systems.\n6. Suggested improvement: a shared-world adventure example with headless authority and snapshots.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**, in the required order:\n\n1. Best aspect: clear cooperative roles and complete-expedition requirements.\n2. Unclear aspect: validating human pacing without human testers.\n3. Hardest task: integrating devices, companions, checkpoints and online lifecycle.\n4. Suggested change: separate automated acceptance from human pacing and presentation judgments."}}
